`ShoppingCartFacadeImpl.modifyCart` checks for a null result immediately after `shoppingCartService.getByCode`; it returns null so `ShoppingCartApi` maps the missing cart to `404` before evaluating the candidate. For an existing cart, it applies the change in memory, builds post-change available items, obtains the subtotal from the shared `OrderService` helper, evaluates the candidate without saving, throws `InvalidDiscountException` when it does not apply (mapped to `400`), and leaves the earlier code untouched. When it applies, it sets `promoCode` to the evaluation's canonical stored code, saves, and returns the cart. Matching is case-insensitive; `promoAdded` is never written. The `updateCartItems` path (current line ~663) and both existing add-item `item.getPromoCode()` paths (current lines ~767 and ~933) are transactional: they apply the item change in memory, evaluate with the shared contract, restore the earlier `promoCode` and save without raising when a candidate fails, and save once with the canonical code when it succeeds. `DiscountServiceImpl.evaluate` is transactional, so managed Product categories and lineage are available through the normal product-service repository path without a custom fetch query.
