Define `DiscountConflictException` and `InvalidDiscountException` in `sm-core` package `com.salesmanager.core.business.exception` as plain message-only `RuntimeException` subclasses with no dependency on `sm-shop`. `RestErrorHandler` maps them to `409` and `400`. Catch `DataIntegrityViolationException` and wrapped constraint violations on discount save or flush and rethrow `DiscountConflictException`, so concurrent duplicate writes also return `409`.
